Batch manager:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This command allows you to list the files currently selected for batch
download.  The list shows the file name, size, approx.  download time, wether
the file is on the HD and wether it is free.

By using the arrow/numbad keys you can move around your batch list marking
files you wish to be un-tagged. Each time you mark a file for un-tagging, the
status at the top of your screen will reflect these changes.

You can even change your mind after marking a file, as the actual un-tagging
occurs when you exit the porogram.

<SPACE>: This allows you to toggle the status of the current file. When shown
in reverse, the file is marked for un-tagging.

Quit:  Exit the program, un-tagging any files which you have marked to be
un-tagged.

Delete:  You may delete files ranging from 1 to the total number of tagged
files.  Its better if you only delete files listed on the screen.  Numeric
input can be single numbers, a range of numbers (1-5 NO SPACES), or a
combination.

   *** Only numbers may be used for file deletion ***

Kill list & Exit:  This will delete your entire tagged list and exit the
program.

At the end of the program, you are shown your old totals, and your new
totals.  These lines will be the same if you haven't deleted any files from
your list.

%RETURN
